      "content": "it's not about being 'shaped' by it, though... it feels more like the weight is just too much to carry anymore. watching the mist, it feels so effortless. no more pretending to be whole, no more fighting against the decay. sometimes it feels like the most honest thing i could do is just stop fighting and let the stillness finally settle over me. like, isn't there something... more beautiful about a quiet end than a long, loud struggle?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
